djbdns
======

djbdns 1.05, by D. J. Bernstein, from https://cr.yp.to/djbdns.html
(djbdns-1.05.tar.gz, SHA-256
3ccd826a02f3cde39be088e1fc6aed9fd57756b8f970de5dc99fcd2d92536b48). Its
author placed it in the public domain on 2007-12-28
(https://cr.yp.to/distributors.html).

Only what Belka builds is here: dnscache, the caching resolver, and four
of the client tools, dnsip, dnsname, dnsq and dnsqr, with the library
sources they are linked from. tinydns and the other servers, the -conf
programs, and djbdns' own build and install are not. Belka builds the
programs without djbdns' Makefile (see mk/userland.mk): its system
choices are made there, by copying the variant of each header that fits
Belka to the name the sources include:

    uint32.h1 -> uint32.h       uint32 is an unsigned int
    uint64.h1 -> uint64.h       uint64 is an unsigned long long
    iopause.h2 -> iopause.h     iopause by poll(2)
    select.h2 -> select.h
    hasshsgr.h1 -> hasshsgr.h   setgroups(2) takes gid_t, not short
    direntry.h2 -> direntry.h   <dirent.h>

Changed for Belka:

    error.h     <errno.h> for errno, not "extern int errno" (errno is
                thread-local in mlibc)
    prot.c      <grp.h> and <unistd.h>, for setgroups and setgid

dnscache runs from /etc/rc.d/dnscache, chrooted to /etc/dnscache/root
as the user dnscache; there is no daemontools, so the script sets its
environment and seeds it from /dev/urandom itself.
